Third-party code in the sbc-emu binary

The sbc-emu binary statically links two crates from crates.io besides the project's own crates
(`cargo tree -p sbc-emu -e normal,build` lists them). Each is available under several licenses;
sbc-emu uses them under the MIT license, whose text and notices follow. The crates from esp32sim
(riscv-rv32/, espressif/) carry their own LICENSE files next to this one.

